      "description": "A player\u0027s mana pool holds exactly this mana (CR 106.4). Written the way a mana cost is \u2014 \u0022{G}{G}\u0022, \u0022{2}{U}\u0022 \u2014 and read as a total, not an order: a pool is a bag of symbols, so the expectation compares what is in it and not how it got there. The empty string is an empty pool. This is what a \u0022add {G} to your mana pool\u0022 card should assert; the event it logged says only that mana changed, which is true of a card that added the wrong colour."
